    {
      "id": "phrase-hacer-un-trio",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "hacer un trío",
      "questionEn": "How do you say that three people have sex together?",
      "answerEn": "Use hacer un trío, changing hacer for the people and time.",
      "noteEn": "This is a fixed expression: hacer is not translated literally as ‘make.’ Hacer changes, as in hacemos for ‘we do’ or hicieron for ‘they did,’ while un trío stays unchanged.",
